she's had conflicts with an iconic star  she loves the role she's lesser known  for she was casting spells while  fighting breast cancer there's a lot you  may not know about the lovely maggie  smith keep watching to learn more about  this beloved dame today's audience might  see maggie smith's work on the harry  potter movies as the high point of her  career however the actress has worked  with the biggest industry stalwarts of  several generations her flying start  began with an early partnership with  cinema legend lawrence olivier it  wouldn't be too much to call olivier the  equivalent of tom cruise leonardo  dicaprio and johnny depp for his time he  has a whopping 85 acting credits to his  name that spanned from the 1930s all the  way to the late 80s he also had a keen  eye for talent according to michael  covney's book maggie smith a biography  olivier was so entranced by smith's  performance in the play the double  dealer that he personally invited her to  join his theater company in major roles  unfortunately smith's strong personality  frequently clashed with oliviers as  company told the mirror the pair soon  became quote professional rivals larry  used to say there was a merry war  between us the conflict led to an  altercation in the middle of a  problematic performance of the 1965 play  othello in a later scene in the play  olivier playing a fellow was supposed to  slap smith according to accounts by  company and smith olivier actually hit  smith knocking her out  when it comes to acting awards for  actresses several famous names and  characters tend to come to mind  considering maggie smith's career which  began in the 1950s there are hardly any  noteworthy acting awards she's yet to  achieve a complete list of awards won by  smith would be longer than this video  itself however some of the major  highlights include two oscars for her  roles in the prime of miss jean brodie  and california suite she's also received  five baftas four emmys and a tony award  for lettuce and lovage smith's honors  even transcend traditional acting awards  most famously the actress was made a  dame commander of the order of the  british empire in 1990 according to  vogue smith was also named a companion  of honor in 2014  maggie smith's love life has had nearly  as much drama as her storied career in  1967 smith married celebrated actor  robert stevens unfortunately their  marriage was not a happy one and the two  got divorced through a mutual agreement  in 1975 smith remarried playwright  beverly cross the pair had fallen in  love years earlier but cross was already  married at the time when they finally  came together the pair enjoyed more than  two decades of wedded bliss until  cross's untimely passing the actress  still feels the loss of her second  husband keenly as she admitted to the  telegraph it seems a bit pointless going  on one's own and not having someone to  share a life with despite the turbulence  of her marriage to stevens smith did  have two children with her first husband  both their sons followed their parents  footsteps and entered the entertainment  industry chris larkin born christopher  stevens decided to change his surname  before entering the industry out of a  desire to make it without getting work  based on his parents fame evidently this  approach paid off as he's been working  steadily in films and movies since 1995  meanwhile his brother toby stevens has  been working in a range of production  since 1992 he has appeared in movies  british television stage plays and even  a bollywood film  while maggie smith has long been  hollywood's go-to actress whenever you  need someone who can shrivel up their  co-stars with a single sharp gaze fellow  actress judy dench can always command a  room as well not only is dench a fellow  dame but she and smith have been close  friends for several decades the duo met  and became firm friends when they were  both up and coming members of london's  old vic theater apparently despite being  known as the soul of professionalism  smith told ew the pair of veteran  actresses laughed so much when they're  together they struggled not to break on  camera the idea of the two dames being  friends has tickled the fancy of the  public so much that their relationship  inspired a documentary 2018's tea with  the dames features smith and dench  together with their fellow dames and  veteran actresses eileen atkins and joan  plowright while very little actual tea  features in the special the name of the  beverage refers to the golden nuggets of  gossip that the dames occasionally  divulged during the course of their  conversation  generally accepted to be one of the most  talented actresses in the world maggie  smith's arresting eyes make up an  integral part of her commanding  on-screen presence the actress's  well-known protuberant gaze can make  anyone on the receiving end feel  automatically inferior and even guilty  for no reason that was part of what made  smith such an effective professor  mcgonagall it turns out the actress's  slightly bulging eyes are a result of  her battles with an immune system  disorder called graves disease the  disorder results in an overproduction of  thyroid hormones that can have a variety  of physical manifestations according to  an interview with the new york times  smith was diagnosed with a condition in  1988 at the age of 54. one of the  symptoms smith suffered from was the  protrusion of the eyes also known as  graves ophthalmopathy which left her  eyes painfully sore smith told the times  magazine that she went through quote 12  months of near isolation which included  radiotherapy and eye surgery to keep the  symptoms under control  while the harry potter movies are  generally renowned for hitting the nail  on the head with casting most of the  characters from jk rowling's iconic book  series maggie smith's portrayal of  minerva mcgonagall is considered  particularly fitting with her witch's  robes spectacles and perpetually strict  expression smith's mcgonagall looks to  have stepped straight out of the books  whenever she appears on screen opposite  daniel radcliffe's harry potter for  radcliffe and smith their bond was  established a year before a single frame  of the first harry potter movie was ever  shot in 1999 the two actors starred  together in a two-part bbc television  drama adaptation of charles dickens  iconic 1850 novel david copperfield  radcliffe played the younger version of  the titular character while smith  assumed the role of betsy trotwood while  the world of david copperfield is far  removed from harry potter the two had an  important correlation for radcliffe in  an interview on the late show with  stephen colbert radcliffe explained that  smith played a big part in getting him  the titular role in harry potter but  maggie  was the person that like recommended me  for potter and so she's the reason i  ended up doing that with the harry  potter films mainly centered around  harry and his friends smith's main  responsibility in the film was to look  strict and occasionally take points off  gryffindor it turns out smith was not  the only actor on set who was chafing  about the one note nature of their role  a fellow sufferer was alan rickman who  played the controversial character  severus snape like smith rickman was  usually only required to stand in the  back and react with a scowl at whatever  harry happened to be doing at the moment  the job got so monotonous that smith and  rickman used to have a hard time trying  to squeeze out different reactions for  the same shot smith told npr that when  the kids shots were filmed she and her  peers would need to film dozens of  different reactions which could get  quite arduous after a while  for the rest of the world actors like  maggie smith and ian mckellen are  serious thespians who only exist to  produce one remarkable performance after  another like their virtuosic  predecessors one day these legends will  retire having left an irreparable mark  on the industry the truth is veteran  actors are regular people who have known  each other for decades as they cross  paths through their work it's no  surprise that such old friends are not  above pulling each other's legs when ian  mckellen was hosting saturday night live  one of the bits that proved the most  popular was when mckellen dressed up as  maggie smith during a weekend update  session alongside jimmy fallon  the best supporting actress who's that  not me whether i win it or not okay i  understood  smith's reaction to the bit was just as  mcgonagall as you can expect during an  interview with the evening standard the  actress remarks that she was afraid of  going to see mckellen's one-man show  because she feared he'd do an impression  of her she went on to add he does them  all the time i rather acidly told him  that i'd done one of him but people  didn't know him well enough to recognize  it unfortunately smith's hopes of  avoiding mckellen's impression of  herself were dashed when he busted  another one out during an interview with  graham norton  graves disease was not the only serious  illness that maggie smith had to contend  with in her life in the late 2000s the  actress was diagnosed with breast cancer  ever the inspiration smith continued to  work even while she was receiving  chemotherapy to deal with the illness in  fact she filmed mcgonagall's scenes for  harry potter and the deathly hallows in  the middle of her treatment the wig she  wore helped disguise the fact that her  natural hair had fallen out due to the  effects of the chemotherapy smith has  also stated that she had to hold on to  the railings next to her in her scenes  because she was too weak to stand  unsupported despite her weakened health  smith fought hard and finished filming  the last potter movie in doing so she  got to film her character's most  triumphant scene her epic battle with  severus snape in the great hall  thankfully smith's treatment worked and  she was able to return to her regular  life  for the current generation of audiences  maggie smith will forever be known as  professor mcgonagall from harry potter  or violet crowley from downton abbey  smith was perfectly cast in both roles  and the countless fans who delighted to  see her play those parts over so many  years might be saddened to hear the  actress herself is not particularly fond  of either of them never one to mince her  words smith made her feelings clear  during an interview for the evening  standard she explained that while she's  incredibly thankful for the opportunity  to perform in both harry potter and  downton abbey the work itself wasn't  particularly gratifying she told es it  wasn't what you'd call satisfying i  didn't really feel i was acting in those  things while fans might disagree with  her smith has played a great range of  leading and supporting roles over a  storied career filled with complex and  fascinating characters that an actor can  really sink their teeth into compared to  those mcgonagall and crawley can seem a  bit one note still smith mentions that  the one thing she particularly enjoyed  about doing the harry potter movies was  how thrilled her grandchildren were by  the fact that she was a part of that  magical world  these days maggie smith is long past the  age when most professionals begin  contemplating retirement but despite  having already achieved everything an  actor could possibly achieve in the  field smith shows no signs of slowing  down in fact the actress intends to keep  working as long as the roles keep coming  unfortunately for smith her rampant  success has made aspects of her private  life fairly difficult she does not seem  to like divulging personal information  to the public eye and she told the  telegraph she can no longer travel alone  without being mobbed by fans despite the  long hours and the endless gaze of the  public smith told the sunday times she  would miss the atmosphere on set too  much if she ever chose to retire from  acting she explained when you're not  working it's scary and when you are  working it's scary because you don't  know if you've got the energy to get  through the day the bleakness of not  doing it and missing out on the  friendships that you make is too much to  bear fortunately age has proved no  obstacle to smith lighting up the screen  with her presence and if fans are lucky  they can expect to see many more  outstanding performances in the coming  years  what an invigorating prospect check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about maggie  smith are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]

